CVE-2026-40973

# CVE-2026-22731: Spring Boot Actuator health group path auth bypass (fixed in 3.5.12 / 4.0.4; enterprise-only)
CVE-2026-22731

# CVE-2026-22733: Spring Boot Actuator CloudFoundry auth bypass (fixed in 3.5.12 / 4.0.4; CloudFoundry not used in platform)
CVE-2026-22733

# CVE-2026-41695: Spring Data Commons DoS via crafted property (fixed in 3.5.12 / 4.0.6; enterprise-only)
CVE-2026-41695

# CVE-2026-41716: Spring Data Commons DoS due to cache (fixed in 3.5.12 / 4.0.6; enterprise-only)
CVE-2026-41716

# CVE-2025-41232: Spring Security authorization bypass on private methods (fixed in 6.4.6; method security not used on private methods)
CVE-2025-41232

# CVE-2025-41248: Spring Security authorization bypass (fixed in 6.4.10 / 6.5.4)
CVE-2025-41248

# CVE-2025-22228: Spring Security BCryptPasswordEncoder max password length (fixed in 6.4.4; password length enforced at API validation layer)
CVE-2025-22228

# CVE-2026-22732: Spring Security Web policy bypass (fixed in 6.5.9 / 7.0.4; enterprise-only / unreleased in Maven Central)
CVE-2026-22732

# CVE-2025-41249: Spring Framework annotation detection vulnerability (fixed in 6.2.11)
CVE-2025-41249

# CVE-2026-41850: Spring Framework SpEL DoS (fixed in 6.2.19 / 7.0.8; enterprise-only; user SpEL expressions not evaluated)
CVE-2026-41850

# CVE-2026-41842: Spring Framework static resource resolution DoS (fixed in 6.2.19 / 7.0.8; static resources served by nginx frontend)
CVE-2026-41842

# CVE-2026-41845: Spring Framework XSS in JavaScript escaping (fixed in 6.2.19 / 7.0.8; pure REST API backend, React frontend escapes DOM)
